# Netlify: the app calls /api on its own site and Netlify forwards it to the API server (status 200 = proxy, the
# address bar never changes). Keeps the login cookie first-party, so browsers that block third-party cookies
# (Safari, incognito, Brave...) keep the user logged in. "!" = always forward, even if a file has that name.
/api/*  https://rent-trlapi.runasp.net/api/:splat  200!
